der_own":0.01828,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":12.2,"_gate_insider_buying":0.163,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":16.3,"pf":[],"description_full":"TTM Technologies, Inc. manufactures and sells mission systems, radio frequency (RF) components, RF microwave/microelectronic assemblies, and printed circuit boards (PCBs) and substrates in the United States, Taiwan, and internationally. It operates in three segments, A&D, Commercial, and RF&S Components. The company offers various engineered systems and RF and microwave assemblies; PCBs and IC substrates, custom assemblies and integrated systems, passive and advanced ceramic RF components, hi-reliability multi-chip modules, and beamforming and switching networks; and design-for-manufacturability, PCB layout design, simulation and testing, quick turnaround (QTA) production, and specialized RF assembly and testing. It also provides multi-mode surveillance and weather avoidance radar systems for fixed- and rotary-wing aircraft, Unmanned Aerial Vehicles, and shipboard platforms; AN/APS-153 multi-mode radar; communications suite within the MH-60R/S multi-mission helicopters; and supports maritime surveillance, counter UAS, and advanced air mobility end markets under MOSAIC brand. In addition, the company offers identification friend; monopulse secondary surveillance radars, and air traffic control systems; wired and wireless communication systems; designs, produces, and tests specialized multi-chip RF modules and components; and manufactures off-the-shelf surface mount microwave components. Further, it provides thick-film ceramic substrates, custom designed application specific integrated circuits, and conventional PCBs; custom electronic assemblies; QTA services; and thermal management. The company serves original equipment manufacturers, electronic manufacturing services providers, original design manufacturers, distributors, and government agencies; and aerospace and defense, data center computing, automotive, medical, industrial, instrumentation, and networking markets. TTM Technologies, Inc. was incorporated in 1978 and is headquartered in Santa Ana, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Edwin  Roks B.Sc., M.Sc., Ph.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 18K people. Revenue per employee of $160K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 5%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["TTM Technologies, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $6.2B market cap on $2.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +9% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 5% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 17% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $683,000 of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.1\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.8\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.4\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 93% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9263772939171407},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (84% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.163},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (43% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"TTM Technologies (TTMI) Stock Dropped, What Is Behind The Latest Move?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nasdaq-ttmi/ttm-technologies/news/ttm-technologies-ttmi-stock-dropped-what-is-behind-the-lates","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795133827.241,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.382,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"TTM Technologies (NASDAQ:TTMI) Rebounds: Has The Rout Ended?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/technology/ttm-technologies-nasdaqttmi-rebounds-has-the-rout-ended","date":